{
 "esm": "1.3.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "mosart_channel",
  "description": "MOSART main-channel routing step (stage 2 of the EqESM project): the per-cell Euler step 4 of mosart_physics.F90:Euler (F90:175-209) composed of mainchannelRouting -> Routing_KW (F90:273-348) and updateState_mainchannel (F90:385-402), written as a storage ODE with the pointwise laws imported from ./mosart_templates.esm. Equations, exactly as in the Fortran (RoutingMethod = 1, the only implemented method, F90:280-284): erin = -eroutUp (F90:302-303); with no river network (rlen <= 0) vr = 0 and erout = -(erin + erlateral) (F90:306-308); for an unrealistically small drainage density per channel (areaTotal2/(rwidth*rlen) > 1e6) erout = -(erin + erlateral) (F90:310-312); otherwise the Manning velocity vr = CRVRMAN_nosqrt(rslpsqrt, nr, rr) (F90:313) and erout = -vr*mr (F90:314), with the dry-cell clamp erout = -(erlateral + erin + wr/localdelt) when -erout > TINYVALUE and wr + (erlateral + erin + erout)*localdelt < TINYVALUE (F90:315-317), in which case vr = -erout/mr when mr > 0 (F90:318-320); the groundwater term temp_gwl = qgwl*area*frac (F90:325); dwr = erlateral + erin + erout + temp_gwl (F90:327); d(wr)/dt = dwr (the storage advance wr += dwr*localdelt, F90:189, in continuous limit); updateState_mainchannel (F90:391-401) sets mr = GRMR(wr, rlen), yr = GRHR(mr, rwidth, rwidth0, rdepth), pr = GRPR(yr, rwidth, rwidth0, rdepth), rr = GRRR(mr, pr) when rlen > 0 and wr > 0, and zeroes all four otherwise; and the reach outflow streamflow flow = -erout (the accumulation flow -= erout of F90:201 with the DLevelH2R averaging, in continuous limit) is exported to the assembly for the runoff aggregation. Units per mosart_tstatusflux_type.F90 / mosart_tspatialunit_type.F90: wr [m3]; erin, erout, dwr, erlateral, eroutUp [m3/s]; vr [m/s]; mr [m2]; yr, pr, rr [m]; rslpsqrt [1]; rlen, rwidth, rwidth0, rdepth, areaTotal2 [m2, m, m, m, m2]; nr is the main-reach Manning roughness (SI dimension s/m^(1/3)); qgwl [m/s]; localdelt = Tctl%DeltaT/DLevelH2R/numDT_r(nr) (F90:184). eroutUp is the outflow sum of the upstream gridcells delivered by the rh_eroutUp sparse-matrix gather over the ID/dnID network (F90:158) - a network-topology operation whose per-cell value is a parameter here until the frivinp network data source lands (boundaries.md 2.4). Two deliberate divergences, documented for reviewers: when the areaTotal2 branch fires the Fortran leaves vr stale (unused there), while here vr takes the Manning value; and the Fortran's negative-storage warning (F90:329-334) is a diagnostic, not physics, and is not transcribed. The tests block pins the dry-cell geometry chain GRMR/GRHR/GRPR/GRRR and dry routing branches pointwise (instantaneous tests, time_span {0,0}) plus the one-substep storage trace in the continuous-ODE form, with numeric tuples from the stage-1 instrumentation dumps (stage1/dumps/mosart/gr_chan.csv, crvrman_chan.csv, mosart_euler.csv); the channel stays dry (mr < TINYVALUE) throughout the dumped window, so the nonzero GRHR flood-plain branches await a wetter data window (see README.md (Testing)). Reference: stage1/cesm/components/mosart/src/riverroute/mosart_physics.F90 (mosart1.1.13).",
   "tags": [
    "environmental_transport",
    "mosart",
    "river-routing",
    "hydrology",
    "channel",
    "kinematic-wave",
    "manning",
    "cesm"
   ],
   "created": "2026-10-26T00:00:00Z",
   "authors": [
    "EqESM project contributors"
   ],
   "references": [
    {
     "citation": "Li, H., Wigmosta, M. S., Wu, H., Huang, M., Ke, Y., Coleman, A. M., and Leung, L. R. (2013). A physically based runoff routing model for land surface and earth system models. Journal of Hydrometeorology, 14(3), 808-828. The MOSART (Model for Scale Adaptive River Transport) routing scheme these components transcribe.",
     "doi": "10.1175/JHM-D-12-015.1"
    },
    {
     "citation": "CESM (Community Earth System Model), ESCOMP/CESM, cesm3.0-alphabranch: MOSART river-routing source (mosart1.1.13) - mosart_physics.F90, mosart_driver.F90, mosart_tstatusflux_type.F90, mosart_tspatialunit_type.F90, rof_comp_nuopc/rof_import_export.F90 - the reference implementation these components are transcribed from.",
     "url": "https://github.com/ESCOMP/CESM"
    },
    {
     "citation": "EarthSciModels - the authoritative .esm corpus this component lives in.",
     "url": "https://github.com/EarthSciML/EarthSciModels"
    }
   ]
 },
 "models": {
  "Channel": {
   "expression_template_imports": [
    { "ref": "./mosart_templates.esm" }
   ],
   "variables": {
    "wr": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m^3",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "storage of surface water in the main channel (TRunoff%wr), [m3]"
    },
    "dwr": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m^3/s",
     "description": "change of main-channel water storage (TRunoff%dwr) = erlateral + erin + erout + qgwl*area*frac; the Fortran type comment says [m3] but the code assigns a flux sum and advances wr += dwr*localdelt, so the rate reading is the code's, [m3/s]"
    },
    "erin": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m^3/s",
     "description": "inflow from the upstream links (TRunoff%erin) = -eroutUp, [m3/s]"
    },
    "erout_manning": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m^3/s",
     "description": "unclamped outflow into the downstream links, -vr*mr, [m3/s]"
    },
    "erout": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m^3/s",
     "description": "outflow into the downstream links after the no-river / small-catchment branches and the dry-cell clamp (TRunoff%erout), [m3/s]"
    },
    "vr_manning": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m/s",
     "description": "Manning velocity of the main-reach flow CRVRMAN_nosqrt(rslpsqrt, nr, rr), [m/s]"
    },
    "vr": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m/s",
     "description": "main-reach flow velocity (TRunoff%vr): 0 when rlen <= 0, -erout/mr when the dry-cell clamp fired and mr > 0, the Manning value otherwise, [m/s]"
    },
    "mr": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m^2",
     "description": "wetted cross-section area of the main channel (TRunoff%mr), [m2]"
    },
    "yr": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m",
     "description": "water depth of the main channel (TRunoff%yr), [m]"
    },
    "pr": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m",
     "description": "wetted perimeter of the main channel (TRunoff%pr), [m]"
    },
    "rr": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m",
     "description": "hydraulic radius of the main channel (TRunoff%rr), [m]"
    },
    "flow": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m^3/s",
     "description": "streamflow from the outlet of the reach (TRunoff%flow) = -erout, the Euler accumulation flow -= erout of F90:201 with the DLevelH2R averaging, in continuous limit, [m3/s]"
    },
    "eroutUp": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m^3/s",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "outflow sum of the upstream gridcells (TRunoff%eroutUp), delivered by the rh_eroutUp ESMF SMM sparse-matrix gather over the ID/dnID network (F90:158); a network-topology input that is a plain parameter here until the frivinp network data source lands (boundaries.md 2.4), [m3/s]"
    },
    "erlateral": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m^3/s",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "lateral flow from the hillslope and subnetwork (TRunoff%erlateral, computed by the subnetwork step), [m3/s]"
    },
    "qgwl": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m/s",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "gwl runoff term from glaciers, wetlands and lakes (TRunoff%qgwl, after the mosart_driver m3/s -> m/s /area conversion), [m/s]"
    },
    "rslpsqrt": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 0.01,
     "description": "sqrt of the slope of the main river reach (TUnit%rslpsqrt, from frivinp rslp), [-]"
    },
    "nr": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "s/m^(1/3)",
     "default": 0.03,
     "description": "Manning's roughness of the main reach (TUnit%nr, from frivinp); network file stores a bare number; declared with its SI dimension s/m^(1/3) for dimensional consistency"
    },
    "rlen": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 10000.0,
     "description": "length of the main river reach (TUnit%rlen, from frivinp), [m]"
    },
    "rwidth": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 50.0,
     "description": "bankfull width of the main reach (TUnit%rwidth, from frivinp rwid), [m]"
    },
    "rwidth0": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 200.0,
     "description": "total width of the flood plain (TUnit%rwidth0, from frivinp rwid0), [m]"
    },
    "rdepth": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 2.0,
     "description": "bankfull depth of the river cross section (TUnit%rdepth, from frivinp rdep), [m]"
    },
    "areaTotal2": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m^2",
     "default": 100000000.0,
     "description": "computed total upstream drainage area (TUnit%areaTotal2, from set_areatotal2), [m2]"
    },
    "area": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m^2",
     "default": 10000000.0,
     "description": "area of the local cell (TUnit%area, from frivinp), [m2]"
    },
    "frac": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 1.0,
     "description": "fraction of the cell included in the study area (TUnit%frac, from frivinp), [-]"
    },
    "localdelt": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "s",
     "default": 180.0,
     "description": "local main-channel substep = Tctl%DeltaT/DLevelH2R/numDT_r(nr) (F90:184), [s]"
    }
   },
   "equations": [
    {
     "lhs": "erin",
     "rhs": { "op": "-", "args": ["eroutUp"] }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "vr_manning",
     "rhs": { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "manning_velocity",
       "bindings": { "sqrtslp": "rslpsqrt", "n": "nr", "rr": "rr" } }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "erout_manning",
     "rhs": { "op": "*", "args": [
       { "op": "-", "args": ["vr_manning"] },
       "mr" ] }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "erout",
     "rhs": { "op": "ifelse", "args": [
       { "op": "<=", "args": ["rlen", 0.0] },
       { "op": "-", "args": [
         { "op": "+", "args": ["erin", "erlateral"] } ] },
       { "op": "ifelse", "args": [
         { "op": ">", "args": [
           { "op": "/", "args": [
             "areaTotal2",
             { "op": "*", "args": ["rwidth", "rlen"] } ] },
           1000000.0 ] },
         { "op": "-", "args": [
           { "op": "+", "args": ["erin", "erlateral"] } ] },
         { "op": "ifelse", "args": [
           { "op": "and", "args": [
             { "op": ">", "args": [
               { "op": "-", "args": ["erout_manning"] },
               1.0e-14 ] },
             { "op": "<", "args": [
               { "op": "+", "args": [
                 "wr",
                 { "op": "*", "args": [
                   { "op": "+", "args": ["erlateral", "erin", "erout_manning"] },
                   "localdelt" ] } ] },
               1.0e-14 ] } ] },
           { "op": "-", "args": [
             { "op": "+", "args": ["erlateral", "erin", { "op": "/", "args": ["wr", "localdelt"] }] } ] },
           "erout_manning"
         ] }
       ] }
     ] }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "vr",
     "rhs": { "op": "ifelse", "args": [
       { "op": "<=", "args": ["rlen", 0.0] },
       0.0,
       { "op": "ifelse", "args": [
         { "op": "and", "args": [
           { "op": ">", "args": [
             { "op": "-", "args": ["erout_manning"] },
             1.0e-14 ] },
           { "op": "and", "args": [
             { "op": "<", "args": [
               { "op": "+", "args": [
                 "wr",
                 { "op": "*", "args": [
                   { "op": "+", "args": ["erlateral", "erin", "erout_manning"] },
                   "localdelt" ] } ] },
               1.0e-14 ] },
             { "op": ">", "args": ["mr", 0.0] } ] } ] },
         { "op": "/", "args": [
           { "op": "-", "args": ["erout"] },
           "mr" ] },
         "vr_manning"
       ] }
     ] }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "dwr",
     "rhs": { "op": "+", "args": [
       "erlateral",
       "erin",
       "erout",
       { "op": "*", "args": ["qgwl", "area", "frac"] } ] }
    },
    {
     "lhs": { "op": "D", "args": ["wr"], "wrt": "t" },
     "rhs": "dwr"
    },
    {
     "lhs": "mr",
     "rhs": { "op": "ifelse", "args": [
       { "op": "and", "args": [
         { "op": ">", "args": ["rlen", 0.0] },
         { "op": ">", "args": ["wr", 0.0] } ] },
       { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "wetted_area",
         "bindings": { "w": "wr", "len": "rlen" } },
       0.0
     ] }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "yr",
     "rhs": { "op": "ifelse", "args": [
       { "op": "and", "args": [
         { "op": ">", "args": ["rlen", 0.0] },
         { "op": ">", "args": ["wr", 0.0] } ] },
       { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "channel_depth",
         "bindings": { "m": "mr", "rwidth": "rwidth", "rwidth0": "rwidth0", "rdepth": "rdepth" } },
       0.0
     ] }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "pr",
     "rhs": { "op": "ifelse", "args": [
       { "op": "and", "args": [
         { "op": ">", "args": ["rlen", 0.0] },
         { "op": ">", "args": ["wr", 0.0] } ] },
       { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "channel_perimeter",
         "bindings": { "h": "yr", "rwidth": "rwidth", "rwidth0": "rwidth0", "rdepth": "rdepth" } },
       0.0
     ] }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "rr",
     "rhs": { "op": "ifelse", "args": [
       { "op": "and", "args": [
         { "op": ">", "args": ["rlen", 0.0] },
         { "op": ">", "args": ["wr", 0.0] } ] },
       { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "hydraulic_radius",
         "bindings": { "m": "mr", "p": "pr" } },
       0.0
     ] }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "flow",
     "rhs": { "op": "-", "args": ["erout"] }
    }
   ],
   "tests": [
    {
     "id": "dry_geometry_guard_cell100312",
     "description": "Instantaneous pin of the dry-cell main-channel geometry chain GRMR/GRHR/GRPR/GRRR and the dry routing branches (mosart_physics.F90:441-572, 302-321) from stage1/dumps/mosart/gr_chan.csv row (step 8, ns 3, m 5, last numDT_r substep, gindex 100312): wr = 1.92941771102327012e-12 m3, rlen = 1.44889171899999987e+05 m give mr = wr/rlen = 1.33165072705013531e-17 m2 (nonzero, so the GRMR branch is taken), but mr <= TINYVALUE (1.0e-14) zeroes the whole GRHR/GRPR/GRRR chain: yr = pr = rr = 0 as in the Fortran; and crvrman_chan.csv row (8,3,5,100312) pins the dry routing: rr = 0 zeroes the Manning velocity vr = 0 (F90:406-422), erout = -vr*mr = 0 (the dry-cell clamp cannot fire: -erout_manning = 0 is not > TINYVALUE), so dwr = erlateral + erin + erout + qgwl*area*frac = erlateral = 6.55201404712201227e-17 m3/s (erin = eroutUp = 0, qgwl = 0) and flow = -erout = 0. This is the last dry state of the dumped window (channel wr reaches 1.9e-12 m3 after 8 steps; every cell stays below the TINYVALUE threshold throughout, so the nonzero GRHR branches are not exercised by this data window). time_span {0,0} keeps wr at its initial condition so the chain is evaluated pointwise; the Fortran values are reproduced to round-off (rel 1e-12).",
     "time_span": {"start": 0.0, "end": 0.0},
     "parameter_overrides": {
      "rlen": 144889.1719,
      "rwidth": 93.9573745727539,
      "rwidth0": 469.78687286376953,
      "rdepth": 2.0,
      "rslpsqrt": 0.099498743710662,
      "nr": 0.05000000074505806,
      "erlateral": 6.552014047122012e-17,
      "localdelt": 180.0
     },
     "initial_conditions": {
      "wr": 1.92941771102327e-12
     },
     "tolerance": {"rel": 1e-12, "abs": 1e-24},
     "assertions": [
      {"variable": "mr", "time": 0.0, "expected": 1.3316507270501353e-17},
      {"variable": "yr", "time": 0.0, "expected": 0.0},
      {"variable": "pr", "time": 0.0, "expected": 0.0},
      {"variable": "rr", "time": 0.0, "expected": 0.0},
      {"variable": "vr", "time": 0.0, "expected": 0.0},
      {"variable": "erout", "time": 0.0, "expected": 0.0},
      {"variable": "dwr", "time": 0.0, "expected": 6.552014047122012e-17},
      {"variable": "flow", "time": 0.0, "expected": 0.0}
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "dry_geometry_guard_cell101032",
     "description": "Instantaneous pin of the same dry chain as dry_geometry_guard_cell100312 for a second cell, 101032, with a shorter reach: gr_chan.csv row (step 8, ns 3, m 5, last substep, gindex 101032): wr = 1.21161058167503756e-13 m3, rlen = 5.39392262550703090e+04 m, rwidth = 6.07456207275390625e+01 m, rwidth0 = 3.03728103637695312e+02 m give mr = 2.24625131985675399e-18 m2 with yr = pr = rr = 0; crvrman_chan.csv row (8,3,5,101032): rslpsqrt = 1.41421356237309507e-02, n_r = 5.00000007450580597e-02, erlateral = 4.11433541143830951e-18 m3/s, vr = 0, erout = 0, dwr = erlateral. The Fortran values are reproduced to round-off (rel 1e-12).",
     "time_span": {"start": 0.0, "end": 0.0},
     "parameter_overrides": {
      "rlen": 53939.22625507031,
      "rwidth": 60.74562072753906,
      "rwidth0": 303.7281036376953,
      "rdepth": 2.0,
      "rslpsqrt": 0.01414213562373095,
      "nr": 0.05000000074505806,
      "erlateral": 4.1143354114383095e-18,
      "localdelt": 180.0
     },
     "initial_conditions": {
      "wr": 1.2116105816750376e-13
     },
     "tolerance": {"rel": 1e-12, "abs": 1e-24},
     "assertions": [
      {"variable": "mr", "time": 0.0, "expected": 2.246251319856754e-18},
      {"variable": "yr", "time": 0.0, "expected": 0.0},
      {"variable": "pr", "time": 0.0, "expected": 0.0},
      {"variable": "rr", "time": 0.0, "expected": 0.0},
      {"variable": "vr", "time": 0.0, "expected": 0.0},
      {"variable": "erout", "time": 0.0, "expected": 0.0},
      {"variable": "dwr", "time": 0.0, "expected": 4.1143354114383095e-18},
      {"variable": "flow", "time": 0.0, "expected": 0.0}
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "dry_geometry_zero_guard",
     "description": "Instantaneous pin of the zero-state branches of the main-channel step from the cold-start rows gr_chan.csv / crvrman_chan.csv (step 1, ns 1, m 1, gindex 100312): with wr = 0 the updateState guard rlen > 0 .and. wr > 0 (F90:391-401) fails and mr = yr = pr = rr = 0; the Manning velocity is zeroed by rr = 0 (vr = 0), erout = -vr*mr = 0, dwr = erlateral + erin + erout + qgwl*area*frac = 0 (erlateral = erin = qgwl = 0 in the cold-start row), and flow = -erout = 0. The geometry is the cell-100312 reach of the dry_geometry_guard_cell100312 test; time_span {0,0} evaluates the chain pointwise.",
     "time_span": {"start": 0.0, "end": 0.0},
     "parameter_overrides": {
      "rlen": 144889.1719,
      "rwidth": 93.9573745727539,
      "rwidth0": 469.78687286376953,
      "rdepth": 2.0,
      "rslpsqrt": 0.099498743710662,
      "nr": 0.05000000074505806,
      "erlateral": 0.0,
      "localdelt": 180.0
     },
     "initial_conditions": {
      "wr": 0.0
     },
     "tolerance": {"rel": 1e-12, "abs": 1e-24},
     "assertions": [
      {"variable": "mr", "time": 0.0, "expected": 0.0},
      {"variable": "yr", "time": 0.0, "expected": 0.0},
      {"variable": "pr", "time": 0.0, "expected": 0.0},
      {"variable": "rr", "time": 0.0, "expected": 0.0},
      {"variable": "vr", "time": 0.0, "expected": 0.0},
      {"variable": "erout", "time": 0.0, "expected": 0.0},
      {"variable": "dwr", "time": 0.0, "expected": 0.0},
      {"variable": "flow", "time": 0.0, "expected": 0.0}
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "one_step_accumulation_step2_sub1",
     "description": "One-substep trace in the continuous-ODE form over [0, 3600] (delt = Tctl%DeltaT of the mosart_euler.csv delt column): entry (step 2, ns 1, gindex 100312) wr = 2.61999638886733984e-16 m3 with erlateral = 5.08977293540838200e-19 m3/s, the DLevelH2R mean of the five m-level erlateral values of the step-2/ns-1 substeps in crvrman_chan.csv ((2.40722391106656755e-19 + 3.57544891632578890e-19 + 4.92208665007665035e-19 + 6.43593338063634362e-19 + 8.10817181893655813e-19)/5; erin = eroutUp = 0, qgwl = 0); the exit state (step 2, ns 1) is wr = 2.09431789563375119e-15 m3. The .esm integrates d(wr)/dt = dwr = erlateral continuously; the end state is EXACT, with no scheme gap: the Fortran accumulates wr += erlateral(m)*numDT_r*localdelt per m-level (F90:189, numDT_r = 4 substeps of localdelt = delt/DLevelH2R/numDT_r = 180 s), and Sigma_m erlateral(m)*720 = mean*5*720 = mean*3600 equals the continuous integral mean*3600. The channel stays dry through the step (mr = wr/rlen <= 1.4e-20 m2 < TINYVALUE, so yr = pr = rr = vr = erout = 0 and dwr = erlateral throughout). Algebraic law values are asserted at time 0 (entry state: mr = 1.80827618414136306e-21 m2, dwr = erlateral), the state wr at the span end.",
     "time_span": {"start": 0.0, "end": 3600.0},
     "parameter_overrides": {
